{"abstract":"We propose reinforcement learning (RL) strategies tailored for reasoning in large language models (LLMs) under strict memory and compute limits, with a particular focus on compatibility with LoRA fine-tuning. Building on early policy gradient methods with baseline subtraction, we design critic-free methods that operate on a small, informative subset of output tokens to reduce memory usage and stabilize training. We introduce S-GRPO, a stochastic variant of Group Relative Policy Optimization, and T-SPMO, a token-level prefix matching approach for fine-grained credit assignment. Applied to Qwen2-1.5B, our methods raise accuracy on the SVAMP benchmark from 46% to over 70% and show strong performance on multi-digit multiplication. Surprisingly, full-token GRPO under LoRA fails to improve over the base model, suggesting that selective token-level optimization may act as an implicit regularizer in low-parameter training regimes.","affiliations":[],"arxiv_id":"2504.20834","authors":["Alan Lee","H. Tong"],"availability":{"basis":"arxiv_public_full_text","checked_at":"2026-08-13T12:44:03+00:00","full_text_url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2504.20834.pdf","license":"arxiv-distribution","page_count":8,"pdf_bytes":342869,"status":"available"},"citation_count":7,"content_digest":"72c450b30b997b683f6975dbc0876c8fb470aee8ff0e1a5faece3b83d37b62dd","created_at":"2026-08-13T12:44:03+00:00","doi":"","identifier_observations":[],"institutions":[],"landing_url":"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/0f3b91ae57fa6a7e94794e421509ed4ad04c813a","legacy_ids":[],"migration_provenance":{"source_content_digest":"a7419ae18435f731b6d9325d3bbe0ebae1800da10d0bf146b5d186e1746f1a22","source_schema_version":"global-work-v1"},"openalex_id":"","pmcid":"","pmid":"","publication_date":"","revision":1,"schema_version":"global-work-v2","semantic_scholar_id":"","source_urls":[],"status":"active","title":"Token-Efficient RL for LLM Reasoning","updated_at":"2026-08-13T12:44:03+00:00","venue":"Semantic S